.TH MERCURY-BROWSER 1 "${MANPAGE_DATE}" "Mercury" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mercury-browser \- launch the Mercury web browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mercury-browser
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ URL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mercury-browser
starts Mercury, an optimized Firefox-based web browser. Browser command-line
arguments are passed to the Mercury executable unchanged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show launcher help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-temp-profile
Start with a newly created profile and delete that profile when Mercury exits.
.TP
.BI \-P " profile"
Start Mercury with the named profile.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " path"
Start Mercury with the profile stored at
.IR path .
.TP
.BI \-\-new-tab " URL"
Open
.I URL
in a new tab.
.TP
.BI \-\-new-window " URL"
Open
.I URL
in a new window.
.TP
.B \-\-private-window
Open a private browsing window.
.TP
.B \-\-safe-mode
Start Mercury in troubleshooting mode.
.TP
.BR \-v , " " \-\-version
Print the Mercury version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mercury/flags.conf
Optional additional command-line flags. If
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset,
.I $$HOME/.config/mercury/flags.conf
is used.
.TP
.I $$HOME/.mercury/mercury-flags.conf
Legacy location for additional command-line flags.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR firefox (1)
.PP
Mercury project page: https://github.com/Alex313031/Mercury
